"في السؤال نقدّم be على الضمير. وفي جواب «نعم» القصير لا نختصر.": "In a question, be comes before the pronoun. In a \"yes\" short answer, don't use the short form.",
"الاسم الذي تحب أن تُنادى به": "The name you want people to call you",
"مع القسم <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">in</span>، ومع الشركة <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">for</span>.": "With a department use <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">in</span>, and with a company use <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">for</span>.",
"نعمل <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">for</span> شركة، ونكون <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">in</span> قسم.": "We work <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">for</span> a company, and we are <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">in</span> a department.",
"المدينة": "City",
"الدراسة": "Studies",
"اسم العائلة": "Last name",
"تقديم شخصين بعضهما لبعض: I'd like to introduce you to …، و This is …، وإضافة معلومة عن كل شخص (works in …، is a director of …)، واستعمال اسم الشخص مبكراً، وسؤال يفتح الحديث (Do you have …?، Is … a big company?)، وعادات التعارف في البلدان.": "Introducing two people to each other: I'd like to introduce you to …, This is …, adding a fact about each person (works in …, is a director of …), using the person's name early, a question to start talking (Do you have …?, Is … a big company?), and customs for meeting people in different countries.",
"تقدّم زميلاً لضيف. ستتعلم:": "You introduce a colleague to a guest. You will learn:",
"إضافة معلومة عن كل شخص.": "To add a fact about each person.",
"استعمال الاسم وبدء الحديث.": "To use the name and start a conversation.",
"شرح القاعدة: المضارع البسيط، وتقديم الآخرين، والأسئلة الشخصية <span class=\"ref\">ص 8–9</span>": "The rules: the present simple, introducing others, and personal questions <span class=\"ref\">pp. 8–9</span>",
"في هذا الدرس تقدّم زميلاً لزائر، وتسأل عن السكن والعمل. نبدأ بالمضارع البسيط الذي نتكلم به عن السكن والعمل، ثم عبارات التقديم، ثم الأسئلة الشخصية البسيطة.": "In this lesson you introduce a colleague to a visitor, and ask about home and work. We start with the present simple, which we use to talk about home and work, then the phrases for introducing people, then simple personal questions.",
"1. المضارع البسيط: أين تسكن؟ أين تعمل؟ <small>(إضافة من خارج الكتاب)</small>": "1. The present simple: where do you live? where do you work? <small>(extra, not in the book)</small>",
"السكن والعمل والدراسة أشياء ثابتة، فنتكلم عنها بالمضارع البسيط. وقاعدته الأساسية تخص <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">he · she · it</span>.": "Home, work and study are fixed things, so we talk about them with the present simple. The main rule is about <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">he · she · it</span>.",
"<b>مع <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">I · you · we · they</span></b> يبقى الفعل كما هو: <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">I live in Riyadh.</span>": "<b>With <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">I · you · we · they</span></b> the verb doesn't change: <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">I live in Riyadh.</span>",
"<b>مع <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">he · she · it</span></b> نضيف <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">s</span>: <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">She works for Delta.</span>": "<b>With <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">he · she · it</span></b> add <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">s</span>: <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">She works for Delta.</span>",
"<b>السؤال:</b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Where</span> + <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">do</span> أو <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">does</span> + الفاعل + الفعل بلا <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">s</span>: <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Where does he work?</span>": "<b>Question:</b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Where</span> + <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">do</span> or <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">does</span> + subject + verb with no <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">s</span>: <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Where does he work?</span>",
"<b>النفي:</b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">don't</span> أو <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">doesn't</span> + الفعل بلا <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">s</span>: <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">She doesn't work here.</span>": "<b>Negative:</b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">don't</span> or <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">doesn't</span> + verb with no <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">s</span>: <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">She doesn't work here.</span>",
"عند تقديم شخص نستعمل <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">he</span> للرجل و <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">she</span> للمرأة: <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">This is Majed. He works in Sales.</span>": "When we introduce someone we use <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">he</span> for a man and <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">she</span> for a woman: <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">This is Majed. He works in Sales.</span>",
"إثبات": "Positive",
"نفي": "Negative",
